# Tests

Match existing Vitest / Playwright layout. When user-visible behavior changes, add or update a test — do not stop at “looks good.”

## Vitest

- Mock dependencies with `vi.mock` before exercising the unit.
- Group with `describe`; name tests by expected behavior.
- Cover success, empty, and error paths for adapters (`error` set vs empty `data`).
- `beforeEach` → `vi.clearAllMocks()`. Prefer `unknown` + narrowing over `any` in new tests.

## Playwright (`client/e2e`)

- Critical user flows only. Prefer role, label, or existing test ids over brittle CSS/XPath.
- Use auto-waiting; no `page.waitForTimeout` / arbitrary sleeps.
- Mock with `page.route` when the test must be deterministic.
- Do not assert visual styles unless that is the ticket.

Do not require Playwright for a non-UI change (adapter-only, CSS token, docs). Do not require a full monorepo test run for a tightly scoped fix — run the relevant package’s tests.
